--
-- price_alert_thresholds — when a sustained price increase becomes an alert.
--   Scope: supplier_id and/or category (products.category); both NULL = the
--   restaurant default. Most specific wins: supplier+category > supplier >
--   category > default > built-in (10% over 21 days).
--   threshold_pct  fraction (0.10 = +10%), 0 < x ≤ 5
--   window_days    look-back window, 7..120
--
-- price_alerts — one detected trend ("tomatoes +18% over 3 weeks") for a
--   (product, supplier), deduped by dedupe_key (restaurant:product:supplier:last
--   observation day) so the daily sweep never re-alerts the same observation.
--   cheaper_* = the same product's latest price at another supplier, when lower.
--   Prices are shekels NUMERIC(12,4) like price_history.unit_price.
--
-- RLS: enabled + per-restaurant policies at the end of this file. Additive only;
-- rollback = DROP TABLE price_alerts, price_alert_thresholds.
